<%- include('partials/head') %>
<body class="ph-body">
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>

  <section class="ph-page-hero">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <div class="ph-eyebrow">Feature deep-dive</div>
      <h1 class="ph-page-title">Recommendations that respect you.</h1>
      <p class="ph-page-lede">Four-way ratings train an on-device model. The picks under your queue come with a reason. The model never leaves your phone.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2>The four-button rating system.</h2>
        <p>Most apps give you one knob: a star or a heart. PodHaven gives you four signals, because "didn't like it" and "actively don't want to hear that podcast again" are different things.</p>
        <ul class="ph-checklist">
          <li><strong>Love</strong> — strongly boost similar episodes</li>
          <li><strong>Like</strong> — gently boost similar episodes</li>
          <li><strong>Dislike</strong> — push similar episodes down</li>
          <li><strong>Not Interested</strong> — removes this episode from the recommendation candidate pool. It's a <em>view</em> filter, not a training signal — it doesn't push the model in any direction</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Rate from the episode detail page, the long-press context menu on any list, or the expanded Play Bar — wherever you are when the verdict hits.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <div class="ph-phone">
          <div class="ph-phone-screen">
            <img src="/public/images/podhaven/episode-rating.png" alt="Long-press context menu showing the four rating options: Love, Like, Dislike, and Not Interested." loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-section-alt">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature ph-feature-flip">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2>An on-device semantic model.</h2>
        <p>Using Apple's on-device NaturalLanguage embeddings, PodHaven turns each episode's title, show notes, and metadata into a vector, then learns what your ratings mean in that semantic space. The math runs on your device. The model never travels to a server. The data never gets sold.</p>
        <p>That privacy isn't just principled — it's a feature. Recommendations stay tuned to <em>your</em> taste, not to whatever is trending in your demographic cohort — and every pick shows its work, with a Recommendation score and the reasons it surfaced.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <div class="ph-phone">
          <div class="ph-phone-screen">
            <img src="/public/images/podhaven/recommended-episode-detail.png" alt="A recommended episode's detail page showing a Recommendation score of 58% and the reason chips Similar to others, Preferred podcast, and Fresh." loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title">Reasons-why you can trust.</h2>
      <p class="ph-lede">Open any recommended episode and its detail page shows a <strong>Recommendation score</strong> (as a percentage) and the tags that explain why it surfaced. No black box.</p>
      <div class="ph-grid">
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Similar to others</h3>
          <p>The episode sits close, in semantic space, to the ones you've rated up.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Preferred podcast</h3>
          <p>You've rated other episodes from this show positively, so the whole show carries weight.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Fresh</h3>
          <p>A recency boost, calibrated to each show's natural cadence (daily / weekly / monthly / evergreen).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Recommendation score</h3>
          <p>One number at the top of the episode, shown as a percentage. The strongest pick reads near 100%, so you can tell a sure thing from a long shot.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-section-alt">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2 class="ph-section-title">Tunable, not just-trust-us.</h2>
        <ul class="ph-checklist ph-checklist-wide">
          <li><strong>Recommendation Diversity</strong> — in <em>Settings → Recommendations</em>, choose <em>Focused</em> to keep picks close to shows you've already rated, or <em>Exploratory</em> (the default) to strip out the structure that encodes a show's <em>format</em> and open up topical discovery across shows you haven't tried.</li>
          <li><strong>Podcast Affinity</strong> — a 0–50% dial (default 10%) for how much a show's track record counts versus an episode's own content similarity. Lower leans pure content; higher leans toward shows you already enjoy.</li>
          <li><strong>Show 0–20 recommendations</strong>, or turn them off entirely. Found in <em>Settings → Up Next</em>.</li>
          <li><strong>Auto-play the top recommendation</strong> when your queue empties, so you never hit silence.</li>
          <li><strong>Per-podcast freshness cadence</strong> — set how fast the freshness boost decays for each show. Daily for news (boost gone within a day), Weekly / Monthly for typical shows, Evergreen for back-catalog content where age is irrelevant. <a class="ph-inline-link" href="/podhaven/guides/per-podcast-settings#freshness">Per-podcast settings guide →</a></li>
          <li><strong>Partial-listen feedback.</strong> If you bail on an episode 3 minutes in, that's a signal. PodHaven tracks listening coverage as a bitmap and feeds it back into the model.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <div class="ph-phone">
          <div class="ph-phone-screen">
            <img src="/public/images/podhaven/settings-recommendations.png" alt="Settings → Recommendations showing the Recommendation Diversity control (Focused / Exploratory) and the Podcast Affinity slider." loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-cta-section">
    <div class="ph-container ph-cta-block">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title ph-section-title-center">Train it on your taste.</h2>
      <p class="ph-lede ph-lede-center">Rate ten or fifteen episodes and the queue starts knowing what to play next.</p>
      <div class="ph-cta-row ph-cta-row-center">
        <span class="ph-cta ph-cta-primary ph-cta-disabled" aria-disabled="true">App Store — coming soon</span>
        <a class="ph-cta ph-cta-secondary" href="https://discord.gg/cMCJeuVY2f" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the Discord</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
